```python
DECL_LINE = re.compile(
    r"^(?:@\[[^\]]*\]\s*)?(?:noncomputable\s+)?(?:private\s+|protected\s+)?"
    r"(theorem|lemma|def|abbrev|structure|instance)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_'.]*)",
    flags=re.M,
)
```
Note: attributes can span multiple lines (`@[simp]\nlemma ...`) — my regex with `@\[[^\]]*\]\s*` handles `@[simp] lemma` on one line and `@[simp]\nlemma` (the `\s*` matches the newline) ✓. Multi-line attribute contents with newlines inside brackets: `[^\]]*` matches newlines too ✓. But `^` anchors at line start; after `@[...]\s*` we can be on the next line ✓.

